{
  "comment": "MyPaint brush file",
  "version": 3,
  "description": "Water",
  "notes": "TOOL, operator `water` (rapier_op 1). A brush of clean water: it thins what is there and lets what goes into suspension wander, so a mark pales and its edge feathers into the paper. It never lays the selected colour and it never puts pigment on blank paper. On a LIVE wash it deposits water with no pigment at all and the wet solver moves what is there (the back-run a painter makes on purpose).\n\nAuthor: Rapier\nLicense: AGPL-3.0-only",
